# oldgames.pkgs — running games from the era of the hardware.
#
# ⚠ WINE IS NOT THE ANSWER TO EVERYTHING, and reaching for it first is the usual
# mistake. Three different problems get three different tools:
#
#   · DOS games          → dosbox-staging. Wine cannot run a DOS binary at all;
#                          it is a Windows compatibility layer, not a PC one.
#   · LucasArts / Sierra → scummvm, which reads the original data files and
#     point-and-click        needs neither Wine nor DOS.
#   · Windows 9x/XP      → wine, with the caveats in docs/old-games.md.
#
# ⛔ SafeDisc and SecuROM WILL NOT WORK, by anything here. They shipped kernel
# drivers, and no compatibility layer emulates a Windows ring-0 driver. A disc
# with either needs a patched executable or a GOG re-release; this is a wall,
# not a configuration problem.
dosbox-staging
scummvm
winetricks
# Getting at the contents of old installers without running them — useful when
# a setup.exe refuses, and often faster than fighting it.
innoextract
cabextract
p7zip
# Some games poll for a real optical drive rather than reading a mounted path.
cdemu-daemon
cdemu-client
# ⛔ .bin/.cue CANNOT BE MOUNTED. A .bin is raw 2352-byte sectors — headers and
# error correction included — where a filesystem expects 2048-byte blocks, so
# mount(8) sees noise. bchunk converts it; cdemu presents it as a real drive.
bchunk
# The Thunar actions report through zenity, because an action that fails
# silently from a right-click menu cannot be told from one that did nothing.
zenity
